Fill the modified-by notice Microchip's banner leaves as a placeholder.

Microchip PK2CMD licence clause 1(b) permits distributing a modified version
for use with Microchip products provided a fixed copyright and modified-by
notice is prominently posted where end users will see it. Upstream's own
`-?l` banner already prints that notice text, but with Microchip's literal
`[INSERT YOUR NAME, DATE OF SOFTWARE MODIFICATION HERE]` placeholder, which
satisfies nothing. This patch names the modifier, so the banner carries a
complete notice rather than a template. To be offered upstream by the human
so the queue can shrink.

--- a/pk2cmd/cmd_app.cpp
+++ b/pk2cmd/cmd_app.cpp
@@ -3371,7 +3371,7 @@
 	printf("\n");
 	printf("\"Copyright (c) 2005-2009 Microchip Technology Inc. All rights\n");
 	printf("reserved. This version of the PICkit(tm) 2 PK2CMD Software has been\n");
-	printf("modified by [INSERT YOUR NAME, DATE OF SOFTWARE MODIFICATION HERE].\n");
+	printf("modified by the epic8 project (2026-09).\n");
 	printf("You may use, copy, modify and distribute the Software for use with\n");
 	printf("Microchip products only.  If you distribute the Software or its\n");
 	printf("derivatives, the Software must have this copyright and disclaimer\n");
